---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/article.css';
---
<SiteLayout page="accommodation" home={false}>
<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="wrap">
  <span class="kicker">Home visits</span>
  <h1>Massage at your accommodation, from Sagres to Lagos</h1>
  <p>You're on holiday. Driving somewhere, parking, finding the place and driving back is an hour you didn't plan for. So the table travels instead: I bring it to your villa, Airbnb or guesthouse, set up in whatever room has the space, and you don't leave the house.</p>
  <p>It's the same treatment I give at <a href="index.html#visit">Mandala in Sagres</a>. Same hour, same price. The only thing that changes is who does the driving.</p>

  <h2>Where I come to</h2>
  <p>The whole stretch of coast between Sagres and Lagos, both included:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sagres</strong> and Vila do Bispo</li>
    <li><strong>Raposeira</strong>, Figueira and Hortas do Tabual</li>
    <li><strong>Budens</strong> and Salema</li>
    <li><strong>Burgau</strong>, Praia da Luz and <strong>Lagos</strong></li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Travel is included in the price.</strong> No call-out fee, no surcharge for the far end of the map — a treatment in Lagos costs exactly what a treatment in Sagres costs. If you're staying somewhere just outside this list, message me anyway and I'll tell you honestly whether I can get there.</p>

  <h2>What you can book</h2>
  <p>Everything on the menu travels. <a href="what-is-abhyanga.html">Abhyanga</a> with warm herbal oils, deep-tissue sports massage, the combination of both, or targeted head, neck and upper body work. If you're not sure which, <a href="ayurvedic-vs-sports-massage.html">ayurvedic vs sports massage</a> explains the difference, and the combination is what most people end up choosing.</p>
  <p>Every treatment is 60 minutes and 50€, wherever it happens.</p>
  <p>One practical note: the ayurvedic treatments use warm oil, and generously. Plan on a shower afterwards rather than going straight out to dinner — which is one of the quieter arguments for having it done where you're staying.</p>

  <h2>Staying at Casa dos Amigos</h2>
  <p>Guests at <a href="https://www.casadosamigos.net/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Casa dos Amigos in Budens</a> can book a treatment during their stay — either ask the house to arrange it or message me directly. It's the same 60 minutes and the same 50€ as anywhere else.</p>
  <p>If you're hosting guests elsewhere along this coast and want to offer the same thing, get in touch.</p>

  <h2>Staying more than a few days</h2>
  <p>If you're here for a week or longer, the <a href="index.html#pass">Recovery Pass</a> is four treatments for 150€, valid three months. It works out at one free treatment, and it's the usual choice for longer stays, repeat visits and anyone surfing several days in a row.</p>

  <h2>Booking</h2>
  <p>Message me on WhatsApp with where you're staying and roughly when suits you. We’ll discuss the pressure and focus when we meet, and adapt the session to you.</p>
  <p>I work in German, English, Spanish, French and Portuguese, so use whichever is easiest. <a href="about.html">More about me</a> if you'd like to know who's turning up.</p>

  <div class="cta-box">
    <p>Every treatment is 60 minutes · 50€, at your accommodation anywhere between Sagres and Lagos. Travel included.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/351938132927?text=Hi%20Tabea!%20I%27d%20like%20to%20book%20a%20massage%20at%20my%20accommodation%20%3A%29" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book on WhatsApp</a>
  </div>
</main>
</SiteLayout>

<style is:global>
  /* Match the primary font's character width while it downloads. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: "Cormorant Accommodation Fallback";
    src: local("Times New Roman"), local("Times"), local("Liberation Serif");
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400 600;
    size-adjust: 95.4%;
  }
  :root {
    --font-heading: "Cormorant Garamond", "Cormorant Accommodation Fallback", Baskerville, Georgia, serif;
  }
</style>
